{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTraceRepBasis","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTraceRepBasis","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTraceCyclicity"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.gram_symm_of_rep_decomp_of_basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.gram_symm_of_rep_decomp_of_basis","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/BilinearTraceRepBasis.lean#L91-L108","doc":"**Gram symmetry from a basis-level representation decomposition.**\n\nThe usable form of `gram_symm_of_rep_decomp`: the decomposition hypothesis is\ndischarged on basis vectors only. Multiplicativity of the `ρ l` on the bilinear\nproduct `B` is unchanged — at `H₄` it is `map_mul` for the Wedderburn `AlgHom`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.rep_decomp_of_basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.rep_decomp_of_basis","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/BilinearTraceRepBasis.lean#L48-L89","doc":"**A linear map's trace-decomposition is determined on the basis.**\n\nIf `τ` and every `ρ l` are additive and homogeneous, then the decomposition\n`τ x = ∑_{l ∈ s} w l · tr (ρ l x)` holding on the basis vectors `e i` forces it\nfor every `x`.\n\nThis is the rung that lets a concrete level discharge `#ι` scalar equations in\nplace of a statement quantified over `ι → R`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}